.SH NAME
md_docs_2CONTRIBUTING \- Contributing to Max-oS 
.PP
We love your input! We want to make contributing to this project as easy and transparent as possible, whether it's:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Reporting a bug
.IP "\(bu" 2
Discussing the current state of the code
.IP "\(bu" 2
Submitting a fix
.IP "\(bu" 2
Proposing new features
.IP "\(bu" 2
Becoming a maintainer
.PP
.SH "We Develop with GitHub"
.PP
We use GitHub to host code, to track issues and feature requests, as well as accept pull requests\&.
.SH "Code Standard"
.PP
To keep the code understandable please make sure it is formatted and readable\&. Please look in the coding style \fBdocs\fP for more information\&.
.SH "We Use <a href='https://guides\&.github\&.com/introduction/flow/index\&.html' >GitHub Flow</a>, So All Code Changes Happen Through Pull Requests"
.PP
Pull requests are the best way to propose changes to the codebase (we use \fCGitHub Flow\fP)\&. We actively welcome your pull requests:
.PP
.IP "1." 4
Fork the repo and create your branch from \fCmaster\fP\&.
.IP "2." 4
If you've added code that should be tested, add tests\&.
.IP "3." 4
If you've changed APIs, update the documentation\&.
.IP "4." 4
Clean up the code: clear any debug code, make sure no warnings are generated when compiling, etc\&.
.IP "5." 4
Ensure the kernel builds and runs\&.
.IP "6." 4
Issue that pull request!
.PP
.SH "Report bugs using GitHub's <a href='https://github\&.com/briandk/transcriptase-atom/issues' >issues</a>"
.PP
We use GitHub issues to track public bugs\&. Report a bug by \fCopening a new issue\fP; it's that easy!
.SH "write bug reports with detail, background, and sample code"
.PP
\fCThis is an example\fP of a bug report someone wrote on stack overflow\&.
.PP
\fBGreat Bug Reports\fP tend to have:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
A quick summary and/or background
.IP "\(bu" 2
Steps to reproduce
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Be specific!
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Give sample code if you can\&. \fCThis stackoverflow question\fP includes sample code that \fIanyone\fP with a base R setup can run to reproduce what I was seeing
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
What you expected would happen
.IP "\(bu" 2
What actually happens
.IP "\(bu" 2
Notes (possibly including why you think this might be happening, or stuff you tried that didn't work)
.PP
.PP
People \fIlove\fP thorough bug reports\&.
.SH "License"
